release_note = "Rectified per review comments (C3/C4/C6/C8/T1). (1) Upgraded jenkins/jenkins:2.541.3-lts-jdk17 to jenkins/jenkins:2.580.2-lts-jdk21, the current LTS, multi-arch amd64/arm64. 2.580.2 fixes the high-severity Jenkins core issues in the 2026-10-28 advisory (CVE-2026-117612, -117613, -117614, -117615, -117616, -117617) and moves the runtime to Java 21. Existing JENKINS_HOME data is compatible: back up first, update plugins after the core upgrade, and roll back by restoring the backup and the old tag if a plugin is not yet compatible. (2) Added a complete PRIVACY.md covering stored data, retention, user rights, security measures, deletion and every third-party endpoint, and linked it from help. (3) Disabled Jenkins usage statistics and telemetry by default with -Dhudson.model.UsageStatistics.disabled=true; documented the update centre, the Google connectivity check, Docker Hub and job/plugin traffic. (4) The app now opens /login (HTTP 200) instead of /, which returns 403 before login, so the App Center self-test can open it; the health check probes the same page. (5) README, CHANGELOG, NOTICE and LICENSE updated."
important    = "First start: open the app, read the initial admin password from DockerAppData/jenkinsdocker/var_jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword, finish setup and change it. Data stays in that folder and survives restarts/updates; back it up before uninstall. Runs as uid 1000. Usage statistics and telemetry are disabled; updates need internet. Plain HTTP on the LAN - use a TLS reverse proxy. Credentials are encrypted, but the key is in the same folder: protect the data directory and its backups."

